  "title": "Integral Relations among Totient Sections",
  "subject": "Erdős #249",
  "subject_kind": "problem",
  "form": "Problem note",
  "pages": 15,
  "question": "What explicit basis and integral relations does the totient k-kernel have at every integer base, and why does that not decide Erdős #249?",
  "precis": "For integers k≥2 and e≥1, the totient sections n↦φ(k^j n+r) with 0≤j≤e and 0≤r<k^j have an explicit rational basis of dimension k^e+1. Every section is an explicit integer multiple of a retained one, and these reductions generate all integral relations, with unique coefficients. The proof combines the local formula for Euler's totient with a nonsingular evaluation matrix obtained from the Chinese remainder theorem and Dirichlet's theorem. The basis theorem does not decide the irrationality of S=∑ φ(n)2^{-n}.",
  "owns": "the exact finite-level totient-kernel basis, independence proof and integral relations; the long paper develops denominator exclusions and other approaches to the binary series",
  "not_authority_for": "the validity of claims tagged Lean, which belongs to the cited kernel-checked source, or a solution to Erdős #249, which remains open",
